{"id": "bart-commercial-parking-permit-recovery", "title": "BART recovered $62,580 for two months of commercial garage use", "seconds": 41.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "made": "2026-11-26", "key": "635564e48476408c", "words": 112, "beats": [{"scene": "garage", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "BART licensed garage space to a company that needed room to store inventory.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.82, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Who", "paid", "for", "the", "extra", "parking", "floor?"], "sub": "A commercial garage agreement"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.43, 0.96, 1.41, 1.88, 2.04, 2.12, 2.56, 2.75, 3.1, 3.39, 3.49, 3.84]}, {"scene": "garage", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "The fourth floor added 298 spaces at 105 dollars per space each month.", "t0": 4.94, "t1": 10.76, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "relationship", "context": "The garage agreement", "heading": "Monthly terms", "source": "report", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Additional fourth-floor spaces", "value": "298"}, {"icon": "fund", "label": "Monthly charge per space", "value": "$105"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.49, 0.89, 1.18, 1.4, 1.73, 2.26, 3.03, 3.26, 3.47, 3.76, 4.09, 4.5, 4.68, 5.14, 5.43]}, {"scene": "garage", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[0]", "established[1]", "suspicious[0]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "The amendment required written notice to extend the extra floor use.", "t0": 10.88, "t1": 14.76, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "San Francisco Bay Area Rapid Transit District, Office of the Inspector General", "text": "Written notice", "mark": "Written notice"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.66, 1.13, 1.48, 1.9, 2.09, 2.54, 2.68, 3.06, 3.43]}, {"scene": "garage", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[0]", "established[1]", "suspicious[0]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "The company continued using the extra floor in May and June without giving that notice.", "t0": 14.88, "t1": 19.51, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "May and June use"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.57, 1.14, 1.46, 1.59, 1.94, 2.29, 2.39, 2.61, 2.74, 3.11, 3.47, 3.79, 4.02]}, {"scene": "recovery", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[2]", "suspicious[1]", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "Two months of fourth floor charges came to 62,580 dollars.", "t0": 19.73, "t1": 25.0, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$62,580", "label": "Underpayment for the two months"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.62, 0.72, 1.07, 1.42, 1.98, 2.24, 2.38, 3.05, 3.56, 3.87, 4.28, 4.61]}, {"scene": "recovery", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[2]", "suspicious[1]", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "The company acknowledged an internal communication error and agreed to a retroactive charge.", "t0": 25.12, "t1": 30.25, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "San Francisco Bay Area Rapid Transit District, Office of the Inspector General", "text": "Second amendment", "mark": "Second amendment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.55, 1.14, 1.29, 1.73, 2.54, 2.93, 3.14, 3.51, 3.62, 3.74, 4.48]}, {"scene": "recovery", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "The later annual report confirms that BART recovered the full amount.", "t0": 30.37, "t1": 34.11, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "annual", "kicker": "San Francisco Bay Area Rapid Transit District, Office of the Inspector General", "text": "Annual report", "mark": "Annual report"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.53, 0.95, 1.39, 1.95, 2.12, 2.44, 2.89, 2.98, 3.24]}, {"scene": "recovery", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "The inspector general did not identify the company publicly.", "t0": 34.23, "t1": 37.45, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Recovery confirmed"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.64, 1.03, 1.22, 1.42, 1.98, 2.1, 2.54]}, {"scene": "recovery", "kind": "end", "ref